{{Quote|An attack on Taanab—though on the Perlemian Trade Route—would earn the dissidents more condemnation than praise, as Taanab's agricultural projects feed billions in the Mid and Outer Rim.|Vice Admiral Dodd Rancit explains why it is unlikely the ''Carrion Spike'' will target Taanab|<ref name="Tarkin" />}}
'''Taanab''' was a [[planet]]<ref name="Smuggler's Run">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref> located in the [[Taanab system]]<ref name="RotJ novel" /> within [[the galaxy]]'s [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]]<ref name="TFABG" /> on the [[Perlemian Trade Route]]. The world was home to several agricultural projects which created [[Foodstuff|food]] used to feed billions of inhabitants of [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] and [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] worlds.<ref name="Tarkin" /> The [[Rebel pilot]] [[Wes Janson]] was [[Reproduction|born]] on Taanab.<ref name="Ultimate SW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

After the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[corvette]] ''[[Carrion Spike]]'' was [[Mission to Murkhana|stolen]] by [[Berch Teller's rebel cell|dissidents]] Taanab was a world within their reach as a potential target, but [[Vice Admiral]] [[Dodd Rancit]] of [[Naval Intelligence Agency|Naval Intelligence]] did not consider the world under threat, as damaging the food source of so many innocents would not fit with the shipjackers' objectives.<ref name="Tarkin" /> By [[10 BBY]],<ref name="Solo date">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]'' establishes [[Dryden Vos]] owned a storehouse on Taanab at the [[time]] of the events of ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' which take place on the ''[[First Light]]'', which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[10 BBY]].</ref> the [[crime lord]] [[Dryden Vos]] owned a storehouse on Taanab which contained items he had [[Collector|collected]].<ref name="Solo Guide">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref>

The [[Standard day|day]] after the [[Battle of Yavin]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] [[Lieutenant]] [[Caluan Ematt]] was [[Ambush on Taanab|ambushed]] by [[Imperial Military|Imperial forces]] on Taanab but managed to flee to the planet [[Cyrkon]] in [[Hutt Space]] before the Empire [[blockade]]d it.<ref name="Smuggler's Run" /> At some point before the [[Battle of Endor]], the [[gambler]] [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] participated in the [[Battle of Taanab]]<ref name="RotJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> where he defeated a [[pirate]] [[fleet]].<ref name="Ultimate SW" />

==Behind the scenes==
In the original story outline for ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', Taanab was a major location in the second half of the movie, where [[Dryden Vos]] and [[Enfys Nest]] would be in a conflict over the world's finite resources. For the movie, Taanab was planned to be a lush jungle environment. Sir [[Wikipedia:Edward James|Edward James's]] surrealist sculpture garden [[Wikipedia:Las Pozas|Las Pozas]], located at the rainforests of central [[Wikipedia:Mexico|Mexico]], was a possible shooting location and design inspiration for Vos' lair.<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

